Both scripts return the same headline figures but 1result.sql is the safer (and therefore correct) choice:

• It first deduplicates bitcoin_prices at the daily level (btc_price CTE).  
  – This prevents a single transaction from being multiplied if more than one BTC price row exists for that date.  
• The rest of the logic (quantity‑weighted average, exclusion of each region’s first year, yearly ranking, YoY %) is identical to 0result.sql.  
• Because 0result.sql skips the de‑duplication step, the join can create duplicate rows whenever multiple BTC price records exist for a given date, inflating totals and biasing the weighted average when duplicate prices differ.

Hence 1result.sql is the more robust implementation.

```plaintext
1result.sql
```